2026-10-06T03:25:16.3407929Z             "body": "## SAF-10: continuous WAL replication (RocksDB) — design, flared, operator, acceptance E2E\n\n**Base is `safety/saf-01-topology-authority` (PR #143's head), not `flare-operator`**, so this diff carries only the SAF-10 work and #143's changes are not re-reviewed here. Merge after #143.\n\n**Draft. Author-run evidence only. Every EV entry stays `unverified` pending its own review. The mechanism is exercised; this is not a statement that it is ready to enable anywhere.**\n\n### What this adds\n- `docs/design-continuous-wal-replication.md`: audit, the coexistence decision (op-level forwarding kept; raw WriteBatch verbatim apply never runs alongside it), two generations (source epoch / receiver incarnation), the common identified-change apply rule, crash-atomic contiguous cursor, positional tombstone GC, serialization, preconditions with counterexamples, STPA additions, acceptance list T1–T17 with per-scenario evidence status.\n- flared (RocksDB): generations, order label captured inside the slot lock, `rl=` identity on forwarded set/delete, one apply rule for both paths, metadata column family, tombstone GC by applied position, follow-mode transport, `handler_wal_follower` (disconnect → resume from the cursor; only history loss → `needs_rebuild`), lifecycle in `cluster`, new stats keys. **Both flags default OFF** (`repl-identity-forward`, `repl-follow-enabled`).\n- operator: ledger ownership (a drop on a WAL-mode follower is HELD and closed by position, never demoted; Unknown holds), follower-declared `needs_rebuild` → repair request, `StateMachine/FollowEvidence` (read / promotion / survival eligibility with Unknown handling, read withholding at commit, candidate shaping for failover and drain, `PROMOTION NOT LOSS-FREE` logging), register SC/EV-16..20, UCA-19..33, STPA controllers A5/A6.\n\n### Evidence\nReports under `docs/reports/2026-09-2*-saf10*`; every run record in `docs/safety-evidence.json` names its tested SHA.\n\n| What | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Acceptance suite `continuous-replication` (13 tests) | PASS locally (runs 10, 11) and on CI |\n| `continuous-replication-purge` (T6) | PASS locally and on CI after the served-gap fix |\n| `continuous-replication-limits` (T9, bounded) | PASS |\n| Full CI matrix, 5 legs, `pull_request` on 41ea98e | [all green](https://github.com/gree/flare/actions/runs/35688265796) |\n| Non-WAL regression suites (30 tests) / RocksDB suites (30 tests) | PASS (3 pre-existing SKIPs) |\n| `flare_unit` / cutter SAF-10 group | 136 checks / 31 tests, 516 assertions |\n\nScenarios staged end to end: normal following; cut with create/update/delete then writes stop, healing resumes from the cursor with no rebuild and no pod recreation; ledger held and closed by position; replica-only stats-fetch failure held as Unknown; `flush_all` → epoch change → `needs_rebuild` → in-place rebuild → follows the new epoch; read eligibility (served only while following, withheld under a cut, restored after healing); three cut/heal cycles; operator restart during a cut; `kill -9` of the replica with a backlog pending (PVC, no full dump); planned promotion through the eligibility gate with the ex-master rebuilding; initial copy under load; retention purge → `lsn_purged` → rebuild; bounded backlog drain with positional tombstone GC.\n\n### Defects the E2E found, all fixed on the branch\n1. `325a2f8` flared: the follower thread returned to the pool on `needs_rebuild`; the later shutdown killed a pooled thread and the reconstruction ran on a dead thread — the rebuild never happened.\n2. `eb2ba17` operator: the master's drop counter was not observed when the replica's stats read failed.\n3. `2379cff` operator: a complete stats reply without follower keys (tch) was treated as unreadable, so drops on non-RocksDB replicas were held forever; stats probes also waited out a 3 s timeout each, pushing a 2-node reconcile to 18–31 s.\n4. `d9d1285` flared: `curr_items` was seeded from `estimate-num-keys` at open, which does not count keys recovered from the WAL — after a crash the count was short by exactly the unflushed tail.\n5. `3b7f38c` flared: RocksDB does not always report a purged position as NotFound; it serves from the oldest surviving WAL file, and the follower refused that as a transient apply error and retried forever. A served gap is now `lsn_purged` → `needs_rebuild`.\n\n### Measurements and limits (please weigh these)\n- **Follow throughput**: the stream stays exactly caught up (lag 0 in every 30 s window) at **300 and 900 keys/s**, and **falls behind monotonically at 2000 keys/s** (lag 35,265 → 294,615 over four minutes), draining in 442 s once the load stops. That matches the ≈1,280 changes/s ceiling measured while draining a 1.24M-change backlog at 2M keys, which is what the default `repl-follow-max-batches` 256 per 200 ms poll allows. Content never diverges — forwarding carries every write — so falling behind is a **position** deficit: replica reads stay withheld, repair entries stay open longer, post-cut catch-up is longer.\n- **The sustained run does not establish disk behaviour**: no memtable flush occurred in the window (768k small records under a 64 MB write buffer), so the flat WAL and data-dir figures are an artefact, and WAL retention for a *trailing* follower was never exercised.\n- **Boot-time exact key scan** (replaces the estimate): 0.48–0.98 µs/key measured at 0.8M / 1.5M / 2.0M keys; ≈8–16 s extrapolated for a 15.8M-key DB. Extrapolation, not a measurement.\n- **Resource floor, not fixed here**: flared's RocksDB defaults budget ≈704 MB (512 MB block cache + 3 × 64 MB write buffers) before flared's own memory. A 512Mi master was OOMKilled 2m42s into a 2M-key load. The chart's node default is `limits.memory: 1Gi` and the CRD exposes no cache/write-buffer knobs, so that floor cannot be lowered through the chart.\n- **T9 is bounded** (15 MB backlog, RSS ≤ 128 MB, tombstones back to zero by position) — not a sustained-load resource test. **T17 (lock-hold / starvation measurement) remains deferred by agreement.**\n- **Rebuild-request routes**: both orders (drop path, follower declaration) have been observed and are pinned sequentially by `flare_unit`; true concurrency within one pass is **not** verified.\n- Failover with the master gone cannot prove currency; the masterless refill's data-bearing last resort can still crown an unfit follower, which is logged as NOT LOSS-FREE. The TCP-side zombie-master guard does not consult follower evidence. A node never yet read is not withheld from reads.\n\n### Parked, not in this PR\nThe background audit agents left unreviewed changes in the working tree; they build and pass (139 checks) but expand scope, so they are parked on `saf-10-audit-followups` (e2ca4c6) for a separate decision: a **new flared-side read guard** (`follow_allows_local_read` + `pre_proxy_read` proxying a not-caught-up WAL replica's reads to the master — overlaps the operator's balance-0 withholding and needs reconciling), a follower **`retry_immediately`** change that polls again whenever the server said MORE even if the whole slice was skipped (a plausible fix for the ceiling above), and a **never-read node is withheld** change that reverses a stated residual and would also affect non-WAL clusters at start-up.\n\n### CI note\n`pull_request` runs were not being created for this PR because it was **unmergeable** (register conflict with the base): GitHub cannot compute the merge commit, so no check suite is produced. Merging the base fixed it and the matrix now runs automatically. Neither branch has required checks or protection, so a green matrix is evidence, not a gate.\n\n### Review guide\n`docs/SAFETY-TODO.md` (SAF-10, 10a–10d, SAF-11), `docs/safety-evidence.json` (EV-03/04/05/13 updated, EV-16..20 new), `docs/STPA-node-state.md` (UCA-19..33, controllers A5/A6), and the reports, which keep every failed run and its diagnosis.\n",
